WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.218 --> 00:00:02.568
- He's the founder of
Swedish high-performance

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:05.516
car manufacturer Koenigsegg Automotive.

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:08.171
He showed interesting
cars from an early age.

00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:10.226
At six years old, he drove a go-kart

00:00:10.226 --> 00:00:11.890
for the first time in his life.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.900
He created the world's fastest road car,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.975
which can go from zero
to 400 kilometers an hour

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.409
in just under 20 seconds.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:20.894
He's Christian von Koenigsegg,

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:23.819
and here are his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:23.819 --> 00:00:24.652
(whooshing)

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:26.639
(thump)

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:28.169
- [Narrator] In only 21 years,

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:29.822
Koenigsegg has come from nowhere

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:32.773
to be one of the highest
regarded hypercar manufacturers,

00:00:32.773 --> 00:00:36.633
being counted alongside Ferrari,
Lamborghini, and Maclaren.

00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:38.757
How have they pulled that off?

00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.628
- Well, we had to work hard,
be a little bit innovative,

00:00:41.628 --> 00:00:45.795
and don't believe in the hype
that it's impossible. (laughs)

00:00:46.882 --> 00:00:49.841
But it's, you know, every day we strive

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.258
and push and learn and adapt.

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:54.884
And when do you do with that for 20 years

00:00:54.884 --> 00:00:57.884
with a great focus within the group,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.191
you can do pretty much anything.

00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:02.633
I think that's the simple answer.

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:04.966
But for sure, it's not easy.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.797
You have to be prepared
to work hard for it.

00:01:08.797 --> 00:01:10.779
From a personal perspective,

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:13.834
my ambition has always been to build cars.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.667
That's why I started my car company

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:18.996
at 22 years of age, 15, 16 years ago.

00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:21.245
And that's all I've been doing since then.

00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:23.301
And then this opportunity presented itself

00:01:23.301 --> 00:01:25.379
to be able to build cars in a larger scale

00:01:25.379 --> 00:01:27.455
with brand that was very dear to me.

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:32.048
And we jumped on this opportunity,
and here we are today.

00:01:32.048 --> 00:01:36.215
So the Koenigsegg group, we
consists of entrepreneurs,

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:39.618
and if you look at all our track records,

00:01:39.618 --> 00:01:42.052
whatever we started, we still have

00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:46.000
and continue with and work
with to make it prosper.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.168
And we have the same ambition with Saab.

00:01:48.168 --> 00:01:51.384
We have gotten into this because
we want to live with Saab

00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:54.513
and work with Saab for a
very long period of time.

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.995
It's not something we do short-term.

00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:57.666
It's a long-term ambition.

00:01:57.666 --> 00:01:59.875
And basically, we don't
do it because it's easy,

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:02.430
we do it because it's a
challenge, it's a real challenge

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.843
and it's a worthwhile challenge

00:02:03.843 --> 00:02:05.312
where we can make a difference.

00:02:05.312 --> 00:02:08.132
- [Christian] Well, as I
mentioned, I have this,

00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:10.844
I saw this Norwegian movie when
I was about five years old.

00:02:10.844 --> 00:02:13.844
And about this guy who built

00:02:13.844 --> 00:02:17.020
a really interesting sports car.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.201
And I remember saying to
myself that when I grew up,

00:02:20.201 --> 00:02:21.585
that's what I want to do as well.

00:02:21.585 --> 00:02:24.704
I want to build my own
car, cars, and sell them.

00:02:24.704 --> 00:02:27.583
So that dream never left me.

00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:31.470
So when I was 19, I
started my first company,

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.373
which was a trading company
to make really big money

00:02:34.373 --> 00:02:37.930
with the ambition to use that
money to build my own cars.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.725
And then when I was 22, I had
made a little bit of money,

00:02:41.725 --> 00:02:44.064
and then I started the car company.

00:02:44.064 --> 00:02:47.896
And that was in 1994,
which was 18 years ago.

00:02:47.896 --> 00:02:49.508
- [Narrator] Koenigsegg
are fully independent

00:02:49.508 --> 00:02:52.289
and manufacture their
cars entirely in-house.

00:02:52.289 --> 00:02:55.998
We asked if this independence
is a benefit to them.

00:02:55.998 --> 00:02:57.197
- I do, I do.

00:02:57.197 --> 00:02:59.708
For example, with the Regera, I don't see

00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:03.875
any of the other established
super hypercar brands daring

00:03:05.058 --> 00:03:07.684
to remove shifting of gears.

00:03:07.684 --> 00:03:09.844
It's such a fundamental thing

00:03:09.844 --> 00:03:11.934
to take away from a sports car.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:16.022
I think it's only Koenigsegg
that could make that decision.

00:03:16.022 --> 00:03:18.683
And I'm very confident about the decision,

00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:22.265
I'm very confident when people
experience that direct power,

00:03:22.265 --> 00:03:25.932
that instant control
you get and directness,

00:03:27.578 --> 00:03:29.912
that they will quickly understand why

00:03:29.912 --> 00:03:31.740
that's a very good
alternative to shifting,

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.517
even though shifting is fun, nice,

00:03:33.517 --> 00:03:36.263
and part of driving a sports car.

00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:41.243
So for example, yeah, we
have more freedoms like that,

00:03:41.243 --> 00:03:43.403
or take more freedoms like that.

00:03:43.403 --> 00:03:47.153
Of course, we want to
infuse Saab with spirit

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:53.414
and kind of make people really
look forward to go to work

00:03:53.414 --> 00:03:56.313
and they can, they feel that
they can make a difference.

00:03:56.313 --> 00:03:58.804
It's basically about empowering people.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.390
Saab is, from the Koenigsegg perspective,

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.532
from a Koenigsegg supercar
company perspective,

00:04:02.532 --> 00:04:05.766
a very large company,
but still, it's people,

00:04:05.766 --> 00:04:08.603
and they're developing
cars on a larger scale.

00:04:08.603 --> 00:04:11.074
So we still think we can get

00:04:11.074 --> 00:04:12.779
that kind of family feeling going,

00:04:12.779 --> 00:04:14.398
but it's mostly important
to empower people

00:04:14.398 --> 00:04:17.556
to know they can make a difference
and really work together.

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:21.341
I see the company as a part of my family.

00:04:21.341 --> 00:04:25.030
And I guess I see our cars
like my children in one way.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.125
I have two sons which I
love very, very, very much.

00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:31.737
But also the cars are my babies somehow.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:34.237
I really care a lot about them

00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:38.365
and it's like a part of myself somehow.

00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:44.407
I don't separate my own being
from the company or the cars.

00:04:44.407 --> 00:04:48.574
We're really connected
together, and it's my life.

00:04:49.643 --> 00:04:52.310
And I don't see my work as work.

00:04:53.347 --> 00:04:54.647
I don't see it as my whole day.

00:04:54.647 --> 00:04:58.104
It's just who I am and what I do.

00:04:58.104 --> 00:04:59.264
I think it's one of our strength.

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:02.556
I mean, there are strength of
being a big car corporation

00:05:02.556 --> 00:05:05.120
with all the resources you have at hand,

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.471
but there are also strengths

00:05:07.471 --> 00:05:10.808
for a small founder-driven
sports car company

00:05:10.808 --> 00:05:15.320
that we have to utilize to
compensate for the lack of size.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.019
So, of course, we heard that all

00:05:18.019 --> 00:05:20.470
the big brands in the
industry were creating

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:24.013
their next-level super
hypercar, hybrid cars,

00:05:24.013 --> 00:05:26.521
and we were not sure what
they were coming out with.

00:05:26.521 --> 00:05:30.021
We were assuming they
want to trump our car,

00:05:30.021 --> 00:05:32.382
the Pagani, the Bugatti, in every aspect.

00:05:32.382 --> 00:05:36.988
And simultaneously, we started
developing the One:1 program,

00:05:36.988 --> 00:05:39.614
so we want to make sure we
overshot what we already did

00:05:39.614 --> 00:05:43.298
by quite a margin, and maybe we brought it

00:05:43.298 --> 00:05:45.376
little bit higher than we
needed to, we will see.

00:05:45.376 --> 00:05:47.950
But I think it will
compare quite favorably

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.450
to these new hybrid hypercars.

00:05:52.914 --> 00:05:56.072
But when it comes to us
competing with the big boys,

00:05:56.072 --> 00:05:58.004
I think that's what
we've always been doing,

00:05:58.004 --> 00:05:59.790
so that's nothing new.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.727
It's really a David against
Goliath kind of scenario

00:06:02.727 --> 00:06:04.719
that we're pretty used
to and are fine with

00:06:04.719 --> 00:06:07.779
and enjoy at the same time, I would say.

00:06:07.779 --> 00:06:09.966
So the motivation to create the One:1,

00:06:09.966 --> 00:06:13.000
even though we already
had a superbly fast car

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.118
that also was good for track use,

00:06:15.118 --> 00:06:18.222
was that some of our
customers really wanted more

00:06:18.222 --> 00:06:20.848
of a cup car, a GT car,

00:06:20.848 --> 00:06:23.206
just specifically developed for the track,

00:06:23.206 --> 00:06:25.070
but they also came with the demand

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.763
that you should have full road usability

00:06:27.763 --> 00:06:31.438
and full homologation, and
that was a bit of a challenge,

00:06:31.438 --> 00:06:33.922
because what we ended up
building was more or less a car

00:06:33.922 --> 00:06:37.889
that looks and feels like
a GT1 car on the track

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:39.576
but then you push a button, it raises up,

00:06:39.576 --> 00:06:41.116
and you have all the creature comforts,

00:06:41.116 --> 00:06:44.323
air conditioning, satellite
navigation, Bluetooth telephone,

00:06:44.323 --> 00:06:49.048
air conditioning, whatever,
that our normal cars have.

00:06:49.048 --> 00:06:50.627
But we have to save weight

00:06:50.627 --> 00:06:52.077
and we have to have more downforce,

00:06:52.077 --> 00:06:53.793
we had to have a stiffer chassis setting

00:06:53.793 --> 00:06:56.898
when needed on the track,
and also lighter weight.

00:06:56.898 --> 00:07:01.861
So yeah, that was the motivation
and that was the challenge.

00:07:01.861 --> 00:07:04.363
Well, I remember when I started that.

00:07:04.363 --> 00:07:06.055
First of all, there were many examples

00:07:06.055 --> 00:07:08.828
of people starting car
companies, extreme car companies,

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:12.249
and not succeeding doing
it for different reasons.

00:07:12.249 --> 00:07:14.861
And I remember saying to myself,

00:07:14.861 --> 00:07:16.391
I have to start when I'm young,

00:07:16.391 --> 00:07:18.260
because it's going to be very difficult,

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.491
it's going to take very long time,

00:07:20.491 --> 00:07:22.712
but I am determined to do it,

00:07:22.712 --> 00:07:25.696
even if it's almost impossible.

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:29.399
And I expected the, I
was coming from Sweden,

00:07:29.399 --> 00:07:32.900
only 22 years old, I
expected everyone to say,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.320
maybe not racing, but that is impossible,

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.596
you will never succeed, it's
just a dream, and so on.

00:07:37.596 --> 00:07:38.954
I expected that.

00:07:38.954 --> 00:07:41.421
So when I got that
response from many people,

00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:42.658
it did not push me down,

00:07:42.658 --> 00:07:45.804
because I was ready for that response.

00:07:45.804 --> 00:07:49.427
And it kind of is, that
triggered me even more to say,

00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:51.459
yes, I understand that you think that,

00:07:51.459 --> 00:07:55.819
but I will show you that
it is actually possible.

00:07:55.819 --> 00:07:59.986
And I get a lot of, now,
feedback and from people around

00:08:01.268 --> 00:08:03.826
who see this and are doing
other things in other areas,

00:08:03.826 --> 00:08:05.347
not only cars, but they say,

00:08:05.347 --> 00:08:08.696
it says, you can do that,
anything must be possible,

00:08:08.696 --> 00:08:10.908
so you made me believe in my dream,

00:08:10.908 --> 00:08:12.348
and now I've done this and succeeded

00:08:12.348 --> 00:08:14.299
and then kind of thank you, whatever.

00:08:14.299 --> 00:08:17.026
And that is so great,
because it actually proves

00:08:17.026 --> 00:08:21.752
that even hypercars can be
very beneficial to society

00:08:21.752 --> 00:08:24.758
because it shows dreams
are possible, in one way.

00:08:24.758 --> 00:08:27.925
So yeah, it's just like that, I guess.

00:08:29.212 --> 00:08:30.493
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:30.493 --> 00:08:34.654
I made this video because
Mopati Bogatsu asked me to.

00:08:34.654 --> 00:08:36.043
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:08:36.043 --> 00:08:37.942
that you want me to profile next,

00:08:37.942 --> 00:08:40.453
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:08:40.453 --> 00:08:42.283
I'd also love to know which of

00:08:42.283 --> 00:08:44.717
the top 10 tips meant the most to you.

00:08:44.717 --> 00:08:45.733
Leave it in the comments.

00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:47.318
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:08:47.318 --> 00:08:48.509
Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:48.509 --> 00:08:51.092
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:08:51.092 --> 00:08:52.636
(whooshing)

00:08:52.636 --> 00:08:54.078
(thump)

